<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prüm Urbar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">893</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Prümer Urbar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Prüm Urbar is a register of the estates, tenants and dues of Prüm Abbey in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eifel">Eifel</a>, drawn up in 893. It lists the abbey's manors and the rents and labour services owed by its peasants, making it one of the most important sources on the manorial economy of the Carolingian world. It survives in a copy made with commentary in 1222 by Caesarius, a former abbot of Prüm.</p></div>
